>> title: Socca
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: chickpeas, french, gluten free, skillet, vegan
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: farinata, cecina, torta di ceci, chickpea pancake
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> step.5: pour into the oiled hot skillet

Heat the #broiler{} with a #cast-iron skillet{} on the top rack.

Whisk @chickpea flour{1%cup}(120 g), @water{1%cup}(240 mL), @fine sea salt{3/4%tsp}(4 g), and @olive oil{2%Tbsp}(30 mL) smooth.

Rest @&(~1)batter{} ~{30%min} so the flour hydrates.

Stir @&(~1)batter{} with @chopped rosemary{1%tsp}(1 g), @black pepper{1/2%tsp}(1 g).

Pour @&(~1)batter{} into the hot skillet slicked with @olive oil for the pan{2%Tbsp}(30 mL).

Broil @&(~1)socca{} ~{8%min} until blistered and set.
